{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>The sons of your mother.</b> And Jacob said to Judah 'sons of your father' — because he had sons from several mothers; but here, since he married only one wife, he says 'sons of your mother' (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Cursed be those who curse you, and blessed be those who bless you.</b> And concerning Balaam it says 'Those who bless you are blessed, and those who curse you are cursed'? The righteous — their beginning is suffering and their end is tranquility, and their cursers and afflicters precede their blessers; therefore Isaac put the curse of cursers before the blessing of blessers. The wicked — their beginning is tranquility and their end is suffering; therefore Balaam put blessing before curse (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:47.902640799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}